==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|sv|de|Gestalt}}. Attested since 1623.

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|c}}

# {{senseid|sv|figure}} a [[figure]] ((shape of a) being, especially a human or human-like being)
#: {{ux|sv|de centrala '''gestalterna''' i berättelsen|the central '''figures''' (characters) in the story}}
#: {{ux|sv|en lång '''gestalt''' skymtade i dimman|a tall '''figure''' could be seen through the mist}}
# {{lb|sv|more rarely|somewhat|poetic}} a [[shape]], a [[form]] (more generally)
# a {{l|en|gestalt}} (a whole different from the sum of its parts)

====Usage notes====
More everyday-sounding compared to English ''gestalt'' in ({{senseno|sv|figure}}), matching ''figure'' in tone as well.

